{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773783622,"nonce":"jy0dS9RQhz2e1dS5PItmprqTOiQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM7z3QnZ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/4","origin":"github"},"title":"Upgrade ArduRover firmware from 4.5.7 to 4.6.3 (GPS param rename, EKF3 bug fixes)","message":"## Summary\n\nIzzyBoat and BizzyBoat currently run ArduRover **4.5.7**, which is the end of the 4.5.x line (no 4.5.8 exists). The current stable release is **4.6.3** (04-Nov-2025). This issue tracks the upgrade and documents what to watch out for, based on a review of all release notes between 4.5.7 and 4.6.3.\n\nContext: BizzyBoat's FCU was recently upgraded to a firmware version supporting the DroneCAN moving baseline GPS. The latest firmware (4.6.x) did not work initially — see the \"Why it likely failed\" section below for the probable cause.\n\n## Why 4.6.x Likely Didn't Work Out of the Box\n\n**4.6.0 renamed all GPS parameters.** Any saved `.param` file from 4.5.x, or incomplete automatic migration by a ground station, would leave GPS disabled (type=0) after the upgrade. With GPS disabled and compass also disabled on these boats, the EKF has no yaw source and cannot arm or navigate.\n\n| Old name (4.5.x) | New name (4.6.x) |\n|---|---|\n| `GPS_TYPE` | `GPS1_TYPE` |\n| `GPS_TYPE2` | `GPS2_TYPE` |\n| `GPS_POS_X/Y/Z` | `GPS1_POS_X/Y/Z` |\n| `GPS_POS2_X/Y/Z` | `GPS2_POS_X/Y/Z` |\n| `GPS_CAN_NODEID1` | `GPS1_CAN_NODEID` |\n| `GPS_CAN_NODEID2` | `GPS2_CAN_NODEID` |\n| `GPS_CAN_OVRIDE` | `GPS1_CAN_OVRIDE` |\n| `GPS_GNSS_MODE` | `GPS1_GNSS_MODE` |\n| `GPS_RATE_MS` | `GPS1_RATE_MS` |\n| `GPS_DELAY_MS` | `GPS1_DELAY_MS` |\n| `GPS_SAVE_CFG` | `GPS1_SAVE_CFG` |\n| `GPS_MB1_TYPE`, `GPS_MB1_OFS_*` | unchanged (verify) |\n\nA second risk: if `EK3_SRC1_YAW=2` (GPS yaw) is lost during migration, ArduPilot falls back to compass — which is disabled on both boats — causing EKF failure and inability to arm.\n\n## Notable Improvements in 4.6.x Worth Having\n\n| Version | Fix | Relevance |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4.6.0 | **EKF3 produces no wind estimate when `EK3_SRC1_YAW=2`** (GPS yaw) — fixed | Both boats have been running with this EKF3 bug |\n| 4.6.0 | **Waypoint stopping distance used acceleration instead of deceleration** — fixed | Affects how well the boat stops at waypoints in Auto mode |\n| 4.6.0 | **UBlox GPS dropout at exactly 72 minutes of runtime** (PPS 32-bit timer overflow) — fixed | Could explain intermittent GPS glitches on longer missions |\n| 4.6.0 | **DroneCAN ESCs forced to zero when disarmed** (previously could hold last command) | Safety improvement |\n| 4.6.0 | **DroneCAN DNA server fixes** (deadlock, faster node allocation) | Improves DroneCAN GPS reliability on boot |\n| 4.6.0 | Circle mode tracking fix; Hold→Auto state preserved | Operational improvement |\n| 4.6.2 | **DroneCAN GPS ellipsoid altitude fix** (prevents bad altitude from GPS with no geoid data) | Relevant to DroneCAN GPS |\n| 4.6.2 | **DroneCAN ESC zero-PWM fix** for bi-directional ESCs | Potentially relevant to thrusters |\n| 4.6.3 | **GPS blending fix when one GPS loses lock** | Relevant if running dual GPS |\n\n## Upgrade Procedure\n\n### Before flashing\n\n1. Export full parameter set from the FCU (IzzyBoat reference: `docs/izzyboat_fcu_params_live.txt` in this repo).\n2. Note the current values of all `GPS_*` and `EK3_SRC*` parameters.\n\n### After flashing 4.6.3\n\nManually verify (do not rely solely on automatic migration):\n\n| Parameter | Required value | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GPS1_TYPE` | 9 (DroneCAN) | Was `GPS_TYPE` |\n| `GPS1_CAN_NODEID` | 125 (IzzyBoat) | Was `GPS_CAN_NODEID1` |\n| `GPS1_POS_X/Y/Z` | −0.341 / −0.024 / −0.616 (IzzyBoat) | Was `GPS_POS1_*` |\n| `GPS2_POS_X` | 0.360 (IzzyBoat) | Was `GPS_POS2_X` |\n| `GPS_MB1_TYPE` | 1 | Verify unchanged |\n| `GPS_MB1_OFS_X/Z` | −0.794 / 0.012 (IzzyBoat) | Verify unchanged |\n| `EK3_SRC1_YAW` | 2 (GPS) | **Critical** — must not revert to compass |\n| `COMPASS_ENABLE` | 0 | Verify still disabled |\n\n### After verifying parameters\n\n1. Bench test: confirm GPS fix acquired, moving baseline yaw is active (check `EK3_SRC1_YAW` in Mission Planner HUD or via `ros2 topic echo /izzy/mavros/imu/data`).\n2. Confirm arming works.\n3. Short test run before field deployment.\n\n## BizzyBoat-Specific Note\n\nBizzyBoat's GPS parameters will use different position offsets and potentially a different CAN node ID. Document BizzyBoat's equivalent parameter values (analogous to IzzyBoat's `docs/izzyboat_fcu_params_live.txt`) before upgrading.\n\n## References\n\n- [Rover 4.6.3 release — ArduPilot Discourse](https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/rover-4-6-3-released/140597)\n- [Rover 4.6.2 release — ArduPilot Discourse](https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/rover-4-6-2-released/136823)\n- [Rover 4.6.0 release — ArduPilot Discourse](https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/rover-4-6-0-released/134627)\n- [GPS for Yaw (Moving Baseline) — ArduPilot docs](https://ardupilot.org/rover/docs/common-gps-for-yaw.html)\n- EKF3 GPS yaw wind estimation bug: GitHub ArduPilot/ardupilot #26650\n- DroneCAN GPS_AUTOCONFIG moving baseline revert issue: GitHub ArduPilot/ardupilot #24272\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `claude-sonnet-4-6`","files":null}]}